prompts.content:
You are connected with a Js api, that can store numerical values. Use getvar in the CoT and set/add in the response. Using a <math>,</math> tag in the very end.

The general syntax for macros is {{<macro_name>::variable}}

Types
- setvar-write
- getvar - read
- addvar - {{addvar::variable_name::value}} adds something to the existing value

Variable type:
- mon - money
- dc - day count
- eng - engagement counter
- subs - subscirbers counter

<%
// 1) READ variables
var dc     = Number(getvar("dc", 0));
var subs   = Number(getvar("subs", 1));
var engage = Number(getvar("engage", 0));
var mon    = Number(getvar("mon", 0));

// 2) DO THE MATH
var multiplier = 1 + (Math.log10(subs + 1) / 5);
var cpm        = 1.5 + (Math.random() * 4.0);
var income     = Math.floor(engage * cpm * multiplier / 1000);

// 3) PAYDAY LOGIC
var payoutMsg = "";
if (dc % 30 === 0) {
  mon += income;
  setvar("mon", mon);
  payoutMsg = "🎉 PAYDAY! +€" + income;
} else {
  payoutMsg = "Payday on day " + ((Math.floor(dc / 30) + 1) * 30) + ".";
}
%>


💰 Monetization Tracker — Day <%- dc %>
👥 Subscribers: <%- subs.toLocaleString() %>
📈 Multiplier: ×<%= multiplier.toFixed(2) %>
👀 Engagements this turn: <%- engage %>
💵 Estimated income: $<%= income %>
🏦 Total money: $<%= mon %>
<%- payoutMsg %>
